#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:3
msgid "Python: house style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:5
msgid ""
"Two packages are Python: ``freeports_dev`` (the format author's tooling "
"and a pytest plugin) and ``freeports_validate`` (grants, which is mostly "
"shell with a Python front end). The engine is **not** — ``import "
"freeports`` loads the compiled crate, and there is no Python source "
"underneath."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:9
msgid ""
"``ruff`` both lints and formats: ``make lint-python`` and ``make fmt-"
"python``. As with Rust, this page is only what a formatter cannot decide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:13
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:15
msgid ""
"``src/`` layout, not flat — ``packages/<name>/src/<name>/`` — so that "
"what the tests import is the working tree and not the copy ``pip "
"install`` left in the environment. ``pythonpath = [\"src\"]`` in each "
"``pyproject.toml`` is what enforces it, and the comment there says why: "
"without it a change to a module would be checked against the previous "
"release of that module, which is the one way a suite can pass while the "
"code it names is broken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:21
msgid ""
"A subpackage per area once an area has more than one file — "
"``freeports_dev/ci/`` holds ``config``, ``metrics``, ``gate``, "
"``report``, ``render``, ``suites``, ``fingerprint``. The rule is the same"
" as the crate's: the split is for readers, and it may change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:26
msgid "Docstrings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:28
msgid ""
"Numpy style (``napoleon`` is configured for it), and a **module docstring"
" on every module** that does the same job as the Rust ``//!``: what this "
"module is for, and which decision it encodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:31
msgid ""
"The house voice again matters more than the format. "
"``freeports_dev/ci/metrics.py`` is the model: it opens by saying what a "
"metric *is*, then spends three paragraphs on why cost is a property of "
"the metric rather than of the caller — which is the fact a reader needs "
"and no signature carries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:35
msgid ""
"Write the docstring that stops the next person reopening the argument. Do"
" not write the one that repeats the parameter names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:39
msgid "Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:41
msgid ""
"Module-level exception classes, one base per area, named for it — "
"``ConfigError`` and friends. Raised with a message that names the value "
"and the expectation, exactly as on the Rust side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Two things are errors rather than resolutions**, and this is a project-"
"wide instinct worth absorbing: an ambiguity that could be silently "
"resolved usually should not be. A branch matching two class lists in "
"``ci.yaml`` is an error, not a first-match-wins; an unknown key in a "
"configuration file is an error, not an ignored line; an unreachable "
"methodology page is an error, not a pass. A setting that is quietly "
"ignored configures nothing and reports nothing, and the user is left "
"believing it took effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:52
msgid "The shell half"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:54
msgid ""
"``freeports_validate`` is a set of shell scripts with a Python entry "
"point, and that is deliberate: it composes ``gpg``, ``jq``, ``curl`` and "
"``sha256sum``, and a signature has to be computed the same way on "
"everyone's machine or it cannot be verified on anyone else's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:58
msgid ""
"Consequences worth knowing before editing them: the filters are plain "
"``jq`` rather than any higher-level expression language, because the "
"signature is computed over ``yq -y -S 'del(.sign)'`` and ``-S`` is jq's "
"own recursive key sort. An \"equivalent\" rewrite that sorts differently "
"silently invalidates every signature. :doc:`../../../reference/cli"
"/freeports-validate` has the detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:64
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/python.rst:66
msgid ""
"Every setting in these tools is reachable through **all three tiers** — "
"configuration file, environment variable, command line — because that is "
"what the engine does and a tool that supports two of the three is a tool "
"people work around. The precedence and the per-field merge are "
":doc:`../../../reference/configuration/dev-and-validate`."
msgstr ""

